Package: mos-profile-dev
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mos build <mos@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Provides: mos-profile
Conflicts: mos-profile-prod
Description: mos image profile marker -- development
 Ships /usr/lib/mos/profile.conf carrying MOS_PROFILE=dev, the file mosd reads
 to decide the default of access.ssh.enabled. The match is case-sensitive and
 FAILS CLOSED: a missing, unreadable or unknown value resolves to prod, which
 means SSH off.
 .
 This package and mos-profile-prod are two renderings of one immutable file, so
 they conflict by name and an image carries exactly one. Both provide
 mos-profile, which is what a package needing "some profile is installed" can
 depend on.
 .
 There is no Depends. The file describes the image and has no runtime
 relationship to whatever reads it, and the payload carries no ELF whose
 shared-library dependencies a packer could resolve.
